{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CHANGE 1049 MERGED (Gerrit submitted 2026-07-30 18:21:47; landed on origin/main as 271f6eaaa). LLM-Review +1 (PASS, 8 advisory, 0 blocking) and Verified +1, both on patchset 1 — first-pass green, no remediation round needed.\nWorktree synced to the merged commit. NOTE the documented gotcha fired again: 'git merge --ff-only' REFUSED ('Not possible to fast-forward') because Gerrit REBASES on submit, so my local 022875758 is not an ancestor of the merged 271f6eaaa. I did NOT discard local work on that signal alone — I verified the landed content first: transport.py 304, _config_coercion.py 189, the held-out oracle 241, the live test 201, and the self-registration line at adapters/__init__.py:16. All present, then reset --hard.\nAlso worth recording: origin/main did NOT show the commit for ~20s after Gerrit reported MERGED — origin is the GitHub MIRROR and it lags the Gerrit merge. A 'did my change land?' check run immediately after submit can produce a FALSE NEGATIVE. Re-fetch before concluding anything is missing.\n\nTICKET STAYS IN_PROGRESS. The code has landed but two acceptance criteria are NOT met, and closing now would certify work that has not been done:\n 1. The [operator-attested] AC needs a PASSING LIVE run of tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py against the J5 harness, with the output summarised here. The file exists and skips cleanly, but has never executed against a real Jira. Run it by dispatching external-integration.yml on main (that runner is native amd64; an Apple-Silicon workstation cannot boot the harness — three measured attempts in this epic).\n 2. The NameIdentity user-search AC needs a test asserting the DC resolver returns an authoritative identity for a real user and raises BackendAssigneeNotFoundError for an unknown one.\nBoth are live-dependent, which is exactly why they were not satisfiable in this session's environment. They are the first work item for whoever picks this up."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785435773588587001,"uuid":"99eadf14-5d40-48c6-97a1-47613bf1a7d7"}